USOS CSMWrap patch 0024 (2026-10-23): USB keyboard / mouse replug on every boot

Builds on patch 0023 (root HID reconnect, Codex branch fix/win95-root-hid
6fe7526a: POST records each root-port HID device with its identity and a
4 KiB page; the USB disk service port watch of 0022 retires its slot on an
unplug and re-attaches the same device on the same port, reusing the POST
interrupt rings, buffers and list nodes). 0023 only works with the 0022
pool (csmwrap.ini int13_boot_disk_only = true, the Windows 9x flow) and only
after USOSUSB.MPD armed the helper-side watch. 0024:

- records root HID devices on every boot: their controller is registered
  for the port watch without the pool (no "stay running without devices"
  change: such a controller has a device), and one 4 KiB input-context page
  is reserved when there is no pool;
- a second driver of the same port watch: the BIOS timer interrupt
  (usb_check_event -> call32 -> usos_hid_tick on the helper core, with the
  caller waiting) every 100 ms while the helper-side watch is not armed and
  only after POST (HaveRunPost 2). That covers MS-DOS, FreeDOS, Windows
  1.x-3.x, Windows 95/98/Me before or without USOSUSB.MPD and the boot
  loaders. In this mode the watch handles HID only (no stick bring-up, no
  media probe); arming reclassifies every port as in 0022;
- ownership guard: a controller whose DCBAAP no longer points at SeaBIOS's
  device context array, or that is stopped, is never touched again by the
  watch (an OS driver took it over: xhci98, NT/Linux xHCI drivers);
- the device may come back on another root port of a watched controller:
  the offline entry with the same VID/PID/revision and configuration hash
  is chosen after the descriptors are read (same port first);
- retries: a bring-up that fails (port reset, Enable Slot, Address Device,
  descriptors, SET_CONFIGURATION, Configure Endpoint) stays pending and is
  retried in the next two watch passes, each with a new port reset (the
  usosusb root-port debounce + 2 retries); "not ours" (no lost device,
  other identity) is not retried;
- fix in 0022's xhci_usos_ctl_mps: the Evaluate Context input slot context
  named root port 1, and xhci_cmd_submit checks CCS of that port, so an EP0
  packet size change (a full-speed device with bMaxPacketSize0 64) failed
  whenever port 1 was empty; now the device's own port;
- USOSUDSK events 18 (root HID unplugged) and 19 (root HID re-attached, the
  retry count), attach reason 12 (HID bring-up failed); HID re-attaches and
  unplugs count in attaches / detaches.

Not covered: devices behind hubs, a HID device that was not present at POST,
a different model on a lost device's place (identity must match).

Own code. Applies after 0001-0010, 0012, 0014-0023, patch -p1 from the top
of the tree. Part of a MODIFIED CSMWrap made by the USOS project (SeaBIOS
LGPLv3).

